WEBVTT

00:39.620 --> 00:41.121
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

00:41.956 --> 00:43.165
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

01:34.008 --> 01:36.010
EDION

01:42.558 --> 01:44.727
Hey, is this how you
spell "Man-eaters"?

01:44.810 --> 01:45.853
WEE KIL MANN-EETERS

01:45.936 --> 01:49.606
You're asking as if
the rest of the words are
spelled right.

01:51.108 --> 01:52.484
Let me write it.

01:52.568 --> 01:53.902
CREDIT CARD LOAN - PARKING LOT

01:53.986 --> 01:56.655
Why can I never write
even though I can read fine?

01:57.239 --> 01:58.240
I know, right?

01:58.324 --> 01:59.742
WE KILL

01:59.825 --> 02:00.826
There.

02:01.577 --> 02:04.621
You have to put "Man-eaters"
on a new line, or it'll look
bad.

02:05.164 --> 02:06.332
How come?

02:06.415 --> 02:07.416
HANDY

02:07.499 --> 02:09.209
<i>On my office door in Nakano,</i>

02:09.293 --> 02:11.920
<i>it looked as if I
killed and ate men.</i>

02:12.004 --> 02:13.130
I KILL MAN-EATERS

02:13.213 --> 02:15.549
<i>Then there was actually
a murder in town.</i>

02:15.632 --> 02:17.885
<i>Everyone suspected me
and came storming over.</i>

02:18.510 --> 02:23.015
Seems to me people get blindly
aggressive about stuff they
don't understand.

02:24.183 --> 02:25.184
WE KILL MAN-EATS

02:25.267 --> 02:28.103
I messed up because
I was talking!

02:28.729 --> 02:31.106
Now it says "Man-eats."

02:31.607 --> 02:33.942
You're making it sound
like it's my fault.

02:34.985 --> 02:36.862
I'll rewrite it
on the other side.

02:36.945 --> 02:41.325
You should include the other
names so it's easy to
understand. Like Hiruko.

02:41.408 --> 02:43.327
You're the only one
who calls them that!

02:43.410 --> 02:45.704
Mikura called them that too.

02:47.164 --> 02:49.583
THE IMMORTAL ORDER

02:52.461 --> 02:54.797
WE KILL MAN-EATERS, MONSTERS,
MUTANT BEASTS (AND HIRUKO)

02:54.880 --> 02:56.215
TWO MILLION YEN EACH

02:56.298 --> 02:58.217
FOR BEGINNERS!
INTRO TO RIVER FISHING

02:58.884 --> 03:01.970
I hope someone snaps
up our offer quickly.

03:03.138 --> 03:05.724
Since they call
themselves an order,

03:05.808 --> 03:10.646
I thought once we got to the
area, there'd be a flag or sign
on an obvious building.

03:12.022 --> 03:14.608
If it's this quiet,
how are we supposed to find
them?

03:18.028 --> 03:19.905
I got one! Maru, the net!

03:19.988 --> 03:21.240
Wait a sec!

03:33.043 --> 03:35.629
What's with the mysterious face?
Thinking about something?

03:36.130 --> 03:37.256
The King of Hotels?

03:38.882 --> 03:39.883
No.

03:40.634 --> 03:44.138
There's an odd number of fish,
and they're all different sizes.

03:44.221 --> 03:46.598
I was wondering how
we're gonna divide them up.

03:47.433 --> 03:50.144
What's wrong, Sis?

03:52.187 --> 03:56.150
You look so good
when you're quiet.

03:56.233 --> 03:58.235
But you ruin it
as soon as you open your mouth.

03:58.318 --> 04:00.320
Wait! Let me try again.

04:01.155 --> 04:04.074
-Ready.
-No, it's totally different.

04:04.158 --> 04:05.784
Wait, one more try!

04:05.868 --> 04:08.370
No way, you blew your chance!

04:13.292 --> 04:17.379
Hey, there's a weird pair
at the end of the road.

04:17.463 --> 04:19.131
They're not from
that group, are they?

04:19.214 --> 04:21.925
You should probably report it.

04:33.228 --> 04:34.521
Dr. Usami.

04:36.940 --> 04:37.941
What is it?

04:38.025 --> 04:43.071
A couple of people
are loitering around with a
strange sign.

04:43.155 --> 04:47.034
It says something about being
able to kill Man-eaters and
monsters.

04:47.534 --> 04:49.244
They might be
roaming bodyguards.

04:53.749 --> 04:55.209
Bring them to me.

04:57.377 --> 04:58.921
Right, of course.

05:06.512 --> 05:09.306
Looks like we've
made another catch.

05:12.726 --> 05:14.645
This way, please.

05:15.145 --> 05:16.897
Watch your step.

05:18.941 --> 05:20.317
STOP HUMAN EXPERIMENTS

05:20.400 --> 05:21.735
FREE THE PATIENTS

05:28.825 --> 05:30.285
This place…

05:30.869 --> 05:35.624
So, we have some business
with the Immortal Order.

05:35.707 --> 05:37.543
What kind of business?

05:37.626 --> 05:39.044
If you've come for treatment,

05:39.127 --> 05:41.880
you shouldn't think of it
as any ordinary hospital.

05:42.548 --> 05:46.510
I'm here to see the doctor
who offers the treatment.

05:47.094 --> 05:48.595
He's an old
acquaintance of mine.

05:49.721 --> 05:51.974
That's not Dr. Usami.

05:52.057 --> 05:54.351
Maybe he's a new doctor.

05:55.978 --> 05:59.523
Are you people
not from the Immortal Order?

05:59.606 --> 06:02.025
What? No!

06:03.068 --> 06:04.194
What?

06:04.903 --> 06:06.989
Where'd they go?

06:07.072 --> 06:09.116
We lost them.

06:09.199 --> 06:12.369
-This is a waste of time.
-Wait, don't go!

06:12.452 --> 06:14.580
At least hear us out!

06:16.498 --> 06:20.460
Our group is opposed to the ways
of the Immortal Order.

06:20.544 --> 06:21.670
We are called Liviuman.

06:21.753 --> 06:23.380
I am their leader, Mizuhashi.

06:24.214 --> 06:26.717
We saw the sign that you made.

06:27.217 --> 06:30.053
So we brought you
here to discuss it.

06:30.137 --> 06:31.847
Hold on a second.

06:31.930 --> 06:35.392
First things first, we basically
have no idea what the Immortal
Order is.

06:35.475 --> 06:37.477
Are they running
some kind of free hospital?

06:37.561 --> 06:40.897
It may look like a hospital,

06:42.482 --> 06:43.817
but, please, take a look.

06:45.861 --> 06:47.613
It must have been
about a year ago.

06:48.113 --> 06:51.575
I had an injury and went to
the Order for treatment.

06:51.658 --> 06:54.911
But, in the end, they restrained
me and amputated my leg.

06:55.954 --> 06:59.625
Then they attached
this metal leg.

06:59.708 --> 07:03.503
We thought it was one
of Dr. Usami's human
experiments.

07:04.338 --> 07:08.050
Even now, people come from all
over to have their injuries
cured.

07:08.133 --> 07:10.510
But, instead, they are
subjected to the work of the
devil,

07:10.594 --> 07:12.596
and their body parts
are replaced with machines.

07:13.388 --> 07:15.724
That's what the
Immortal Order is.

07:16.350 --> 07:19.311
But since it's called an order,
they must have followers

07:19.394 --> 07:21.855
and people who don't complain
about the treatments, right?

07:21.938 --> 07:23.732
Even before the Collapse,

07:23.815 --> 07:27.903
machines were used to replace
body parts that had
deteriorated.

07:27.986 --> 07:32.783
This led to the idea that the
brain, or its memory data,

07:32.866 --> 07:36.370
could be transplanted into a
robot's body, thus transcending
mortality itself.

07:36.953 --> 07:38.664
From an ethical viewpoint,

07:38.747 --> 07:41.958
it wasn't possible to actually
carry out anything that radical.

07:42.042 --> 07:44.252
But now we live in
a lawless world.

07:44.961 --> 07:47.798
If there are doctors
willing to take their research
that far,

07:47.881 --> 07:51.301
then there are probably people
who would happily become
machines.

07:51.385 --> 07:53.053
I bet you're thinking,

07:53.136 --> 07:56.139
"Why not let those
who want to be involved get on
with it?"

07:56.223 --> 08:00.352
Or, "Isn't it your fault for
going there without knowing what
you were in for?"

08:01.353 --> 08:03.271
I suppose that's what you think.

08:03.355 --> 08:05.273
It's not that…

08:05.357 --> 08:07.526
I understand.

08:07.609 --> 08:10.821
You're probably wondering why
I speak out against their ways.

08:11.905 --> 08:14.950
But I have seen it.

08:16.118 --> 08:18.578
<i>The repulsive reality.</i>

08:38.640 --> 08:41.435
Behind a curtain,

08:41.518 --> 08:43.770
I saw a body completely
chopped to pieces,

08:43.854 --> 08:46.815
hacked up to a point
that ought to be beyond
survival.

08:46.898 --> 08:50.944
A human being kept alive
by an impossible number of
machines.

08:52.446 --> 08:54.656
<i>When it noticed my presence,</i>

08:55.157 --> 08:57.075
<i>it spoke to me.</i>

08:58.702 --> 09:00.078
Let…

09:01.037 --> 09:03.331
Let me die.

09:04.708 --> 09:06.293
Even more shockingly,

09:06.376 --> 09:11.089
that mass of machines, which has
trampled on any remaining human
dignity,

09:11.173 --> 09:14.551
appears to be
an object of worship for them.

09:14.634 --> 09:18.430
So we decided to do
something about it.

09:19.014 --> 09:22.309
<i>Dr. Usami has gained followers</i>

09:22.392 --> 09:25.520
<i>from the knowledge he has
acquired with his inhumane acts.</i>

09:25.604 --> 09:28.482
<i>It's possible that in this era,</i>

09:28.565 --> 09:31.610
<i>their way of doing things
will become the dominant one.</i>

09:32.194 --> 09:34.362
So this guy isn't Dr. Usami?

09:34.446 --> 09:35.947
That's not him.

09:36.448 --> 09:37.991
Usami is younger.

09:39.326 --> 09:40.577
Right.

09:41.620 --> 09:44.080
We heard that the Immortal Order

09:44.164 --> 09:46.792
are transplanting parts of the
Man-eaters onto human bodies.

09:46.875 --> 09:48.168
What?

09:48.251 --> 09:51.129
Really? So that's
what they're doing.

09:53.173 --> 09:56.510
That's connected to
what I wanted to discuss with
you.

09:58.762 --> 10:00.680
<i>It seems that the Immortal Order</i>

10:01.181 --> 10:04.726
<i>is keeping a Man-eater in the
basement of their building.</i>

10:14.861 --> 10:17.280
What are we going to do, Sis?
Shall we do it?

10:18.156 --> 10:19.407
Let's do it.

10:19.491 --> 10:21.493
They said they'd pay us.

10:22.661 --> 10:24.955
If a Man-eater can be
killed, we kill it.

10:25.038 --> 10:26.957
People are going to
get eaten if we don't.

10:27.040 --> 10:28.333
That much is certain.

10:28.834 --> 10:31.670
If you say so, then I will, but…

10:32.504 --> 10:35.131
But what?

10:35.215 --> 10:38.176
You're not as
coolheaded as usual.

10:39.678 --> 10:41.346
You're turning
into Haruki again.

10:41.429 --> 10:42.889
What's that supposed to mean?

10:43.557 --> 10:45.725
I've always been
Haruki in my head.

10:45.809 --> 10:47.060
I am coolheaded.

10:59.322 --> 11:00.824
She was naked.

11:01.908 --> 11:04.327
No, no, stop it.

11:05.161 --> 11:07.038
<i>From Sis's point of view,</i>

11:07.122 --> 11:11.459
<i>it's possible the doctor we're
chasing is part of the Immortal
Order,</i>

11:11.960 --> 11:15.088
<i>which might bring us closer to
the reason why the woman she
loved died.</i>

11:15.714 --> 11:17.924
<i>No wonder it's
hard to keep cool.</i>

11:19.217 --> 11:22.596
<i>But something doesn't feel
right. What is it?</i>

11:24.973 --> 11:26.725
<i>I need to figure it out.</i>

11:30.645 --> 11:35.066
<i>Perfect. Being squished so
close, I can only think of
irrelevant stuff.</i>

11:37.819 --> 11:40.655
As many of you already know,

11:40.739 --> 11:44.200
this morning
another large building
collapsed.

11:44.826 --> 11:49.247
Day by day, the civilization
that we knew is returning to the
earth.

11:49.331 --> 11:51.708
It is useless to us now.

11:51.791 --> 11:55.795
Those of us who remain don't
have the power to rebuild what
is left.

11:56.379 --> 11:59.132
What did machines
bring to humanity?

11:59.215 --> 12:01.009
Tanks! Bombs!

12:01.092 --> 12:02.510
Fighter planes!

12:02.594 --> 12:06.806
What did we get in return for
this poison? Electricity!
Convenience!

12:06.890 --> 12:10.226
What we are left with, as a
result, is an endless winter

12:10.310 --> 12:13.563
and a mountain of debris
just rotting away.

12:13.647 --> 12:15.565
-Yeah!
-Exactly!

12:16.149 --> 12:17.984
This kind of thing

12:18.610 --> 12:19.903
is not needed!

12:21.279 --> 12:23.031
-Our leader!
-Ms. Mizuhashi!

12:23.114 --> 12:24.115
Are you okay?

12:25.492 --> 12:26.952
We don't need machines.

12:27.452 --> 12:29.955
We don't need machines!

12:30.038 --> 12:31.539
-No machines!
-No machines!

12:31.623 --> 12:33.291
BANK OF JAPAN NOTE
TEN-THOUSAND YEN

12:37.128 --> 12:39.547
It's getting really
crazy out there.

12:40.173 --> 12:44.177
All we can do right now
is rant and rave outside their
building.

12:44.260 --> 12:47.722
But if we get rid of that
monster, we can have a
discussion on equal terms.

12:47.806 --> 12:50.058
A discussion, huh?

12:50.642 --> 12:54.145
They could release that monster
anytime. While they have that
secret weapon,

12:54.229 --> 12:57.524
the Order is not
going to listen to us.

12:58.441 --> 13:01.945
Well, we're only
being paid to kill it.

13:02.445 --> 13:04.197
After that, you can
do what you like.

13:04.280 --> 13:08.326
<i>Fine. So, as for today's plans…</i>

13:12.956 --> 13:13.957
RESTORE HUMAN RIGHTS

13:14.040 --> 13:16.710
Stop human experiments!

13:16.793 --> 13:17.794
FREE THE PATIENTS!!

13:17.877 --> 13:20.547
<i>Now, they're demonstrating
against human experimentation</i>

13:20.630 --> 13:23.174
<i>outside the Immortal
Order's building.</i>

13:23.758 --> 13:26.136
<i>But it's a diversion.</i>

13:26.219 --> 13:29.973
<i>We'll use it to get you to the
basement through another
entrance.</i>

13:30.056 --> 13:31.850
<i>There's no guard?</i>

13:31.933 --> 13:35.061
<i>The guard to the basement
is one of our own.</i>

13:35.895 --> 13:37.147
I've heard the plan.

13:43.028 --> 13:44.612
We're counting on you.

14:10.805 --> 14:12.182
It's so bright.

14:12.265 --> 14:13.725
The lights are on.

14:15.143 --> 14:17.145
They must have
some serious power generators.

14:17.729 --> 14:21.900
All that talk of life-support
systems is starting to sound
more credible.

14:25.278 --> 14:27.030
But it's weird, isn't it?

14:27.530 --> 14:31.576
There's no sign of a Man-eater
here. Not a single sound.

14:33.953 --> 14:35.622
Sis?

14:37.415 --> 14:40.543
I've had a weird
feeling for a while.

14:41.461 --> 14:42.879
I think I just got what it is.

14:43.880 --> 14:48.635
It feels like we're being set
up. Just like when we went to
find the water.

14:49.636 --> 14:51.638
What if there are
no Hiruko here?

14:52.263 --> 14:54.808
If there were Hiruko
in this basement,

14:55.433 --> 14:58.603
<i>then why would that old guy
who wanted a transplant</i>

14:58.686 --> 15:01.314
<i>go to all that trouble
looking for Hiruko parts?</i>

15:02.148 --> 15:03.149
No, but…

15:05.443 --> 15:06.736
No, wait.

15:06.820 --> 15:08.154
What you're saying makes sense,

15:08.238 --> 15:12.033
but that guy probably
has never been to the Immortal
Order.

15:12.534 --> 15:15.328
It's pretty likely
he was on a wild chase after
some rumor.

15:15.829 --> 15:20.041
If they just wanted to lock us
up in here, that plan seems way
over-the-top.

15:20.625 --> 15:22.001
Why would they do all this?

15:22.085 --> 15:23.670
To use us for experiments!

15:23.753 --> 15:27.340
If we don't escape, they'll chop
us up and keep us alive like
that forever!

15:29.634 --> 15:33.429
<i>They could use
a gas heavier than air to put us
to sleep.</i>

15:34.097 --> 15:35.682
<i>Is that why we're
in the basement?</i>

15:36.307 --> 15:38.560
This is way too risky, Sis.
Let's get outta here!

15:39.102 --> 15:40.270
Wait!

15:41.938 --> 15:44.482
What is that?

15:50.238 --> 15:54.450
Is it a dormant Man-eater?

15:57.912 --> 15:59.581
Yeah, it's a Hiruko.

16:01.082 --> 16:02.167
Crushed it.

16:06.004 --> 16:08.631
It's weird that I'm glad
there was a Man-eater here,

16:08.715 --> 16:10.675
but looks like
you were worried about nothing.

16:11.509 --> 16:12.510
Right.

16:13.595 --> 16:14.929
Wha-- Sis!

16:15.513 --> 16:17.140
Isn't that one down there too?

16:18.016 --> 16:19.934
Another? What the hell?

16:20.018 --> 16:21.769
I thought there was only one.

16:21.853 --> 16:24.230
There could be more.
We need to cover every corner.

16:32.280 --> 16:33.823
The fact that they're not moving

16:33.907 --> 16:37.118
is actually more annoying.

16:42.624 --> 16:43.999
Got you.

16:44.500 --> 16:46.211
Is this guy the big boss?

16:47.587 --> 16:48.713
Gross.

16:48.796 --> 16:52.217
Did those little ones
multiply from this guy?

16:52.717 --> 16:55.220
But why are they frozen stiff?

16:55.845 --> 16:59.182
When a Man-eater is on the verge
of death, it enters a state of
suspended animation.

16:59.265 --> 17:01.309
They survive by playing dead.

17:01.935 --> 17:06.022
These ones probably haven't had
any food since being trapped
down here.

17:07.190 --> 17:09.067
Right. Food…

17:09.692 --> 17:12.111
And now that two
humans have shown up,

17:12.862 --> 17:14.656
I guess they'll
start to wake up?

17:21.704 --> 17:23.039
There!

17:24.040 --> 17:25.250
Sis!

17:25.333 --> 17:27.001
There's a little
one that's moving!

17:27.085 --> 17:28.836
I don't know if I got it.

17:28.920 --> 17:30.713
Where'd you go?

17:34.467 --> 17:35.677
No.

17:36.386 --> 17:38.930
They've got quick
moves. Watch out!

17:41.099 --> 17:42.183
No way.

17:42.267 --> 17:45.103
They're slipping
through the walls.

17:50.942 --> 17:52.735
Damn it, get off!

17:53.361 --> 17:54.362
Maru, run!

17:55.029 --> 17:56.030
Maru!

18:03.496 --> 18:04.872
Go to hell!

18:12.505 --> 18:13.756
This can't be happening.

18:14.257 --> 18:16.217
Die!

18:16.718 --> 18:18.344
Just die already!

18:18.845 --> 18:21.222
Let me go!

18:47.957 --> 18:49.208
Help.

18:49.792 --> 18:51.627
Help me, Robin!

18:59.302 --> 19:00.470
<i>It's over.</i>

19:01.554 --> 19:02.680
<i>I can't…</i>

19:03.806 --> 19:06.476
<i>breathe.</i>

19:21.407 --> 19:22.408
You're okay.

19:22.492 --> 19:24.702
There's nothing here.
Nothing happened!

19:28.581 --> 19:29.624
Was I dreaming?

19:30.166 --> 19:32.835
That's impossible.
Did it make me hallucinate?

19:33.669 --> 19:35.671
Thank God. You're
back to reality.

19:36.381 --> 19:39.175
I don't know what I'd have done
if you'd stayed like that.

19:40.134 --> 19:43.471
You just started shooting at
nothing and flailing violently
out of nowhere.

19:44.931 --> 19:46.349
Just rest like that for a bit.

19:46.891 --> 19:48.768
I'll deal with the
rest of the Hiruko.

19:52.021 --> 19:53.022
Hey, Sis?

19:55.233 --> 19:57.026
I guess you wanted
Robin to save you.

19:57.610 --> 19:58.611
What?

20:00.113 --> 20:03.491
Sorry, I thought
they'd already got you.

20:12.333 --> 20:13.376
<i>Damn it.</i>

20:13.459 --> 20:16.295
<i>What kind of guy says
something so stupid?</i>

20:17.004 --> 20:19.132
<i>Why exactly should
I be apologizing?</i>

20:30.977 --> 20:32.728
I think that's all of them.

20:33.521 --> 20:35.148
Are you feeling better, Sis?

20:35.731 --> 20:36.732
Yeah.

20:37.233 --> 20:40.445
When you were staring
at that huge Hiruko,

20:40.528 --> 20:42.905
it must have hypnotized you.
I'm sure of it.

20:43.531 --> 20:46.909
That's why I told you
you weren't as coolheaded as
usual.

20:50.455 --> 20:51.789
I'll try and focus more.

21:00.548 --> 21:01.966
-Hey!
-Ouch.

21:02.049 --> 21:04.469
As if you're trying
to sneak another one in!

21:04.552 --> 21:05.970
Are you stupid?

21:08.222 --> 21:09.223
Someone's coming.

21:24.614 --> 21:26.073
Is it dead?

21:26.574 --> 21:27.867
Really?

21:31.829 --> 21:34.290
This guy's clearly bad news.

21:40.213 --> 21:42.924
There's someone else
I want you to kill.

21:45.843 --> 21:48.638
Someone I want you to help.

21:51.015 --> 21:52.683
If we can.

21:52.767 --> 21:55.728
I mean, it depends on
what you're asking.

21:56.395 --> 21:58.397
Aren't you from
the Immortal Order?

21:59.190 --> 22:01.484
I don't remember
ever referring to it that way,

22:01.567 --> 22:03.778
but I've heard it
called that before.

22:03.861 --> 22:06.072
Right.

22:06.155 --> 22:09.659
So, is Dr. Usami here?
We want to see him.

22:10.660 --> 22:12.078
Usami?

22:12.161 --> 22:13.454
That's me.
